# TN Title: Flow Chart / Tree Diagram Generation

## When to Use
After extracting Part V Flow on Title from a CMS TSR, create a visual tree diagram per survey series showing:
- Original parent survey → bifurcation chain → current sub-survey numbers
- Patta numbers at each link
- Party names in ownership chain
- Acquisition status (acquired by SLP/DRA, not acquired, error)

## Sheet Setup
- New sheet called `FLOW_CHARTS`
- 5 columns: A (tree text), B (patta chain), C (party chain), D (status), E (dates/docs)
- One section per survey series (158, 166, 167, 168, 176+177 usually)

## Box-Drawing Characters
Use these for tree structure (never `+` — it triggers formula in Sheets):
- `├──` — branch to child (more children exist)
- `└──` — last child in branch
- `│` — vertical connector for continuation
- `┌──` — first child (for parallel top-level branches)
- Spaces for indentation (4 per level)

